Q: Compute 17 * 23 step by step. Show your work in 2 lines, then give the final answer.
A:  To compute \( 17 \times 23 \):

1. First, break it down using the distributive property: \( 17 \times 23 = 17 \times (20 + 3) = (17 \times 20) + (17 \times 3) \).
2. Calculate each part: \( 17 \times 20 = 340 \) and \( 17 \times 3 = 51 \). Add these together: \( 340 + 51 = 391 \).

The final answer is \( 391 \).

